  "edition_top_html": "<header class=\"mast\">\n  <div class=\"lead\">\n    <div class=\"titlecol\">\n      <h1>Basin Watch</h1>\n      <div class=\"wir\">Week in review</div>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"sub\">Daily Athabasca Basin uranium briefing, covering both juniors and majors, ranked by news-release materiality.<span style=\"display:block;white-space:nowrap\">NR and tenure movement tracked on the companion Basin Explorer map.</span><span style=\"display:block\">A new edition publishes every day at 9:00 a.m. CST.</span></p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"tickerwrap\"><div class=\"ticker\">\n    <span class=\"tksym mono\">U₃O₈</span>\n    <span class=\"tkpx mono\">$124.35</span>\n    <span class=\"tklbl\">CA$/lb</span>\n    <span class=\"tksrc\">Aug month-end avg · US$89.68 at 1.3866</span>\n  </div></div>\n  <div class=\"mastright\">\n    <div class=\"edition\">\n      <div class=\"n mono\">2026-09-12</div>\n      <div class=\"d edd\">Sept 06 – Sept 12</div>\n      <div class=\"d edd\">Edition 003</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</header>\n\n<section class=\"signals\">\n  <div class=\"sig hot\">\n    <span class=\"k\">Metres drilled</span>\n    <span class=\"v mono\">10,159</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">IsoEnergy's 26-hole summer program at Larocque East, completed 8 Sep - strongest core radioactivity yet on the Hurricane South trend, assays pending</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"sig\">\n    <span class=\"k\">Financing raised</span>\n    <span class=\"v mono\">$2.0M</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">Terra Clean Energy's brokered private placement for South Falcon East, general working capital</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"sig\">\n    <span class=\"k\">Geophysical surveys</span>\n    <span class=\"v mono\">2</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">Terra North's 2,441 line-km airborne radiometric survey (completed) and Belmont's ~2,500-station ground gravity program (announced, October start)</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"sig hot\">\n    <span class=\"k\">Lapsing by 19 Sep</span>\n    <span class=\"v mono\">102</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">active dispositions reach their good-standing date inside seven days - 17 to one individual holder, 13 Eagle Plains, 12 Murchison Minerals, 11 Orano</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"sig\">\n    <span class=\"k\">Approaching, 20-26 Sep</span>\n    <span class=\"v mono\">94</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">the next tier out - dispositions reaching good standing 8-14 days from now, worth watching if you're weighing new ground</span>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<h2 class=\"sec\">Ranked by technical materiality</h2>\n\n<div class=\"news\">\n\n  <article class=\"item lead\">\n    <div class=\"rank mono\">01</div>\n    <div class=\"body\">\n      <div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"co\">Purepoint Uranium</span><span class=\"tk\">TSXV:PTU</span><span class=\"when mono\">10 Sep</span></div>\n      <p class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"https://www.juniorminingnetwork.com/junior-miner-news/press-releases/343-tsx-venture/ptu/210693-purepoint-reports-winter-2026-assays-from-dorado-jv-s-nova-target.html\">Purepoint Reports Winter 2026 Assays from Dorado JV's Nova Target</a></p>\n      <p class=\"why\"><b>Still the week's only chemical assay, not just a gamma reading.</b> Nine holes at the Nova discovery on the 50/50 Dorado JV (with IsoEnergy), eastern basin margin. Best result is NV26-05, 0.3 m at <span class=\"g-assay\">1.65% U₃O₈</span> from 390.4-390.7 m, paired with a 61,070 cps average / 73,070 cps peak on the downhole Mount Sopris 2PGA-1000 probe. NV26-03A returned a broader 3.9 m at 0.04% U₃O₈ (412.6-416.5 m) with a 0.4 m higher-grade inclusion at 0.10% U₃O₈, plus a separate 0.4 m interval at 0.79% U₃O₈ (37,050 cps) from 418.2-418.6 m. Seven more holes (NV26-01, -02, -04, -06A, -07, -08, -09A) returned lower-grade mineralization, 0.01-0.07% U₃O₈. Collars are tabulated in NAD83 UTM Zone 13 (e.g. NV26-05 at 548809E, 6475821N). An earlier release from this same winter program (14 April) reported the gamma-probe readings alone with assays pending; this release is the assay follow-through on those same holes. The release ties results to previous Nova drilling of up to 8.1% U₃O₈ over 0.4 m within a broader 1.62% U₃O₈ over 2.1 m, and describes a mineralized corridor extending roughly one kilometre. The summer program at Nova has also been completed, with those results still pending.</p>\n      <div class=\"chips\">\n      <span class=\"chip g\">0.3 m @ 1.65% U₃O₈, NV26-05</span>\n      <span class=\"chip g\">3.9 m @ 0.04% U₃O₈, NV26-03A</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">61,070 cps avg / 73,070 cps peak, NV26-05</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">9-hole winter program, Nova discovery</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">~1 km mineralized corridor, prior drilling to 8.1% U₃O₈</span>\n      <span class=\"chip warn\">summer program results still pending</span>\n    </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"stk\"><span class=\"sx\">TSXV:PTU · CAD · 11 Sep</span><span class=\"sp\">0.36</span><span class=\"sc fl\">0.00%</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>52-WK</b> 0.30 – 0.85</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>VOL</b> 74.4K / 64.6K&nbsp;avg</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>MKT CAP</b> $28.58M&nbsp;·&nbsp;79.4M&nbsp;sh</span></div>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"item lead\">\n    <div class=\"rank mono\">02</div>\n    <div class=\"body\">\n      <div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"co\">IsoEnergy</span><span class=\"tk\">TSX:ISO</span><span class=\"when mono\">8 Sep</span></div>\n      <p class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/isoenergy-completes-summer-drilling-at-larocque-east-intersecting-widespread-and-strongest-radioactivity-to-date-along-the-hurricane-south-trend-302871790.html\">IsoEnergy Completes Summer Drilling at Larocque East, Intersecting Widespread and Strongest Radioactivity to Date Along the Hurricane South Trend</a></p>\n      <p class=\"why\"><b>26 holes for 10,159 m, and every number in the release is a counts-per-second reading, not a grade.</b> The program overran its 8,000 m / 20-hole plan and brings 2026 to 16,963 m in 43 holes. Best intervals are LE26-250 on the West L Fault, 3.5 m at <span class=\"g-cps\">11,075 cps</span> from 341.0 m including 0.5 m at <span class=\"g-cps\">43,160 cps</span>; LE26-273, 3.0 m at <span class=\"g-cps\">14,135 cps</span> from 328.0 m including 1.0 m at <span class=\"g-cps\">36,292 cps</span>; and LE26-254 on the East L Fault, 2.0 m at <span class=\"g-cps\">10,110 cps</span> from 331.5 m. Eighteen of the 26 holes returned at least <span class=\"g-cps\">350 cps</span> over half a metre, 13 exceeded <span class=\"g-cps\">1,000 cps</span>. These are handheld RS-125 spectrometer totals taken on core - not a chemical assay, and not calibrated downhole gamma either, so they cannot be read as a percentage or converted into one. What they do establish is spatial: mineralization is now widespread along the Hurricane South trend rather than confined to isolated holes. Samples are at SRC with no stated turnaround. What's missing: any assay from the summer program, any cps-to-grade correlation for these holes, and a date for either.</p>\n      <div class=\"chips\">\n      <span class=\"chip g\">3.5 m @ 11,075 cps, LE26-250</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">0.5 m @ 43,160 cps, peak reading</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">10,159 m in 26 holes</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">18 of 26 holes ≥350 cps over 0.5 m</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">West and East L Fault, Hurricane South trend</span>\n      <span class=\"chip warn\">handheld cps on core - not a grade, assays pending</span>\n    </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"stk\"><span class=\"sx\">TSX:ISO · CAD · 11 Sep</span><span class=\"sp\">14.75</span><span class=\"sc dn\">-4.10%</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>52-WK</b> 10.19 – 18.47</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>VOL</b> 174.5K / 212.2K&nbsp;avg</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>MKT CAP</b> $962.53M&nbsp;·&nbsp;65.3M&nbsp;sh</span></div>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"item\">\n    <div class=\"rank mono\">03</div>\n    <div class=\"body\">\n      <div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"co\">Terra Clean Energy</span><span class=\"tk\">CSE:TCEC</span><span class=\"when mono\">9 Sep</span></div>\n      <p class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"https://www.juniorminingnetwork.com/junior-miner-news/press-releases/3266-cse/tcec/210525-terra-clean-energy-announces-2-0-million-brokered-private-placement-led-by-centurion-one-capital.html\">Announces $2.0 Million Brokered Private Placement Led by Centurion One Capital</a></p>\n      <p class=\"why\"><b>A modest raise with no catalyst attached.</b> Up to 14,285,714 units at $0.14 (Centurion One Capital as lead agent, 8% cash fee plus broker warrants), with the agent holding an option for a further $300,000. Each unit carries a warrant exercisable at $0.22 for three years, with an acceleration clause if the stock trades above $0.44 for 15 straight days. Proceeds are earmarked for capital expenditures and general working capital rather than a named program at South Falcon East, and the release ties the raise to no specific drill or permitting milestone. Expected to close around 5 October, subject to CSE approval and the standard four-month-and-a-day hold.</p>\n      <div class=\"chips\">\n      <span class=\"chip s\">$2.0M brokered PP</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">14.29M units @ $0.14</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">warrants @ $0.22, 3-yr</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">optional +$300K over-allotment</span>\n      <span class=\"chip warn\">no program or milestone named for proceeds</span>\n    </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"stk\"><span class=\"sx\">CSE:TCEC · CAD · 11 Sep</span><span class=\"sp\">0.14</span><span class=\"sc fl\">0.00%</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>52-WK</b> 0.08 – 0.21</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>VOL</b> 20.5K / 107.6K&nbsp;avg</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>MKT CAP</b> $8.87M</span></div>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"item\">\n    <div class=\"rank mono\">04</div>\n    <div class=\"body\">\n      <div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"co\">Terra North Resources</span><span class=\"tk\">TSXV:GEMC</span><span class=\"when mono\">8 Sep</span></div>\n      <p class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"https://www.juniorminingnetwork.com/junior-miner-news/press-releases/1155-tsx-venture/gemc/210491-global-energy-metals-highlights-identification-of-prominent-radiometric-anomalies-at-charlot-neely-lake-uranium-project.html\">Prominent Radiometric Anomalies Identified at Charlot-Neely Lake</a></p>\n      <p class=\"why\">First look at a new airborne dataset over Terra North's Charlot-Neely Lake ground, about 20 km north of Uranium City. 2,441 line-km of high-resolution radiometric and magnetic survey across 163.7 km² resolved seven uranium-thorium radiometric anomalies, one of them north of Neely Lake where historical outcrop sampling reportedly ran up to <span class=\"g-assay\">0.8% U₃O₈</span>. No anomaly-by-anomaly dimensions or coordinates are given, and radiometrics read surface and near-surface signal only, not depth. The release comes from Global Energy Metals (TSXV:GEMC), which holds a 0.5% NSR royalty across Terra North's Saskatchewan portfolio rather than operating the ground - Terra North itself is private, holds an option on the project from Fulcrum Metals Canada Ltd., and is 39.5%-owned by Terra Balcanica Resources (CSE:TERA).</p>\n      <div class=\"chips\">\n      <span class=\"chip s\">2,441 line-km airborne radiometric + magnetic</span>\n      <span class=\"chip s\">163.7 km² survey area</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">7 radiometric anomalies</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">historical outcrop up to 0.8% U₃O₈, N of Neely Lake</span>\n      <span class=\"chip warn\">radiometric signal only, no drill or depth data</span>\n    </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"stk\"><span class=\"sx\">TSXV:GEMC · CAD · no fresh quote</span><span class=\"sp\">—</span><span class=\"sc fl\">—</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>52-WK</b> —</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>VOL</b> —</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>MKT CAP</b> —</span></div>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"item\">\n    <div class=\"rank mono\">05</div>\n    <div class=\"body\">\n      <div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"co\">Green Canada Uranium</span><span class=\"tk\">TSXV:GCUC</span><span class=\"when mono\">9 Sep</span></div>\n      <p class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"https://www.newsfilecorp.com/release/313517/Green-Canada-Uranium-Mobilizes-Drill-to-Marshall-Project-Athabasca-Basin-Saskatchewan\">Mobilizes Drill to Marshall Project, Athabasca Basin, Saskatchewan</a></p>\n      <p class=\"why\">First drilling under Green Canada's own name, on its first day trading following an RTO. Two holes are planned at the 11,225-hectare Marshall property, roughly 30 km southwest of CanAlaska's West McArthur Pike Zone, testing an unconformity-style target beneath sandstone cover. The company holds Marshall through a 51% option into North Millennium's underlying interest. No metreage, timeline or target dimensions are given - this is a mobilization notice, not a results release. Only two days of trading history exist for this ticker; treat the 52-week range below as a listing-to-date range, not a meaningful annual band.</p>\n      <div class=\"chips\">\n      <span class=\"chip\">2 holes, maiden drill</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">11,225 ha Marshall property</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">~30 km SW of West McArthur Pike Zone</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">unconformity-style target</span>\n      <span class=\"chip warn\">no metres, timeline, or target dimensions given</span>\n    </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"stk\"><span class=\"sx\">TSXV:GCUC · CAD · 11 Sep</span><span class=\"sp\">0.12</span><span class=\"sc dn\">-14.29%</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>52-WK</b> 0.12 – 0.18 (2 days' history)</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>VOL</b> 214.5K / 11.5K&nbsp;avg</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>MKT CAP</b> $2.27M&nbsp;·&nbsp;34.5M&nbsp;sh</span></div>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"item\">\n    <div class=\"rank mono\">06</div>\n    <div class=\"body\">\n      <div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"co\">Belmont Resources</span><span class=\"tk\">TSXV:BEA</span><span class=\"when mono\">10 Sep</span></div>\n      <p class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"https://thenewswire.com/press-releases/1k49F1o03-belmont-resources-to-conduct-ground-gravity-survey-at-crackingstone-uranium-project-saskatchewan.html\">Belmont Resources to Conduct Ground Gravity Survey at Crackingstone Uranium Project, Saskatchewan</a></p>\n      <p class=\"why\">New to this brief. A ground gravity program aimed at an under-tested corner of the historic Beaverlodge district: approximately 2,500 stations on a 50 m × 50 m grid across 253 ha at Crackingstone, about 8 km southwest of Uranium City, scheduled for the first week of October and expected to run 10-14 field days. The company holds a permit for up to 40 drill holes through 2028 and frames the survey as the lead-in to that program. Crackingstone's own historical record, cited in the release, includes showings up to <span class=\"g-assay\">15.6% U₃O₈</span>, with 11 tons mined at <span class=\"g-assay\">2.3% U₃O₈</span> from the No. 7 Adit during the district's original production era - historical figures from past-producing workings, not from any drilling of Belmont's own. This is a mobilization notice for a survey that has not yet run; no gravity data exists yet.</p>\n      <div class=\"chips\">\n      <span class=\"chip s\">~2,500-station ground gravity survey</span>\n      <span class=\"chip s\">253 ha, 50m × 50m grid</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">scheduled first week of October</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">permitted for 40 holes through 2028</span>\n      <span class=\"chip warn\">historical showings to 15.6% U₃O₈ - not Belmont's own drilling</span>\n    </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"stk\"><span class=\"sx\">TSXV:BEA · CAD · 11 Sep</span><span class=\"sp\">0.050</span><span class=\"sc fl\">0.00%</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>52-WK</b> 0.02 – 0.06</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>VOL</b> 128.6K / 136.0K&nbsp;avg</span><span class=\"sr\"><b>MKT CAP</b> $6.62M&nbsp;·&nbsp;132.5M&nbsp;sh</span></div>\n  </article>\n\n  </div>\n\n<div class=\"note\">\n  <span class=\"h\">Majors: an unusually quiet week outside of IsoEnergy's own program</span>\n  <b>CanAlaska Uranium (TSXV:CVV)</b> mobilized a single rig to Key Extension on 8 September, 100% owned, about 15 km south of the Key Lake mill. Six to ten holes are planned to late October, testing up-ice of the Orchid Lake boulder field along a western conductive trend with more than 10 km of sparsely tested conductive stratigraphy. Winter holes KEY017 and KEY018 hit graphitic stratigraphy with semi-brittle faulting and localized chlorite-clay alteration; those geochemical results are still outstanding. Historical Orchid Lake boulder grabs ran up to <span class=\"g-assay\">0.13% uranium</span>, and the release itself flags them as selective and not representative.<br><br>\n  <b>Cameco, Orano, Denison, NexGen and Uranium Energy Corp issued no releases in the window.</b> UEC has been silent since 23 July; the Roughrider pre-feasibility study is still unreleased, with the last substantive status the June quarterly that had drilling roughly 80% complete and Tetra Tech engaged. UEC's fiscal year ends 31 July, so full-year results around October are the next scheduled opening for it.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"note\">\n  <span class=\"h\">Out of basin, but on the watchlist</span>\n  <b>ATHA Energy (TSXV:SASK), 8 September, Rib North at Angilak, Nunavut.</b> Seven holes (RIBN-DD-010 to -016A) extend the mineralized corridor from the 300 m defined at discovery in 2025 to 1.45 km of strike on the eastern limb, open in all directions. RIBN-DD-011 returned 20.0 m of composite mineralization over fifteen zones between 494.0 m and 700.5 m, including a 1.5 m interval at 661.5-663.0 m averaging <span class=\"g-cps\">8,453 cps</span> with a <span class=\"g-cps\">26,680 cps</span> peak; RIBN-DD-013A returned 13.0 m composite over five zones, RIBN-DD-014 7.0 m over six. Every number is a downhole total-count reading from a Mount Sopris 40TGU-1000 probe, not a calibrated eU₃O₈ conversion and not a chemical assay, so none of it converts to a percentage - the company's own thresholds are <span class=\"g-cps\">300 cps</span> for mineralization and <span class=\"g-cps\">10,000 cps</span> for high grade. Angilak is Archean-hosted vein-style mineralization in the Kivalliq, geologically unrelated to the basin. Carried because ATHA holds Gemini and a large basin package; not ranked against basin results.<br><br>\n  <b>Manhattan Uranium Discovery (TSXV:MANU), 10 September, Lisbon Valley, Utah.</b> A compilation of 499 historical drill holes returned a best of <span class=\"g-assay\">3.70% eU₃O₃</span> over 5.2 ft, gamma-derived from legacy data, not new drilling. Sandstone-hosted Colorado Plateau style, unrelated to the basin. Carried because Manhattan operates Murmac and Strike on this roster.\n</div>",
  "edition_bottom_html": "<div class=\"tblwrap\">\n<table class=\"tbl\">\n  <caption>Registry state, week ending 2026-09-12</caption>\n  <thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Now</th><th>Week ago</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>Active dispositions</td><td class=\"num\">7,468</td><td class=\"num\">7,468</td><td>Unchanged by claim count; new staking activity in the trailing 14 days is tracked in the two rows below</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Lapsed register</td><td class=\"num\">368</td><td class=\"num\">368</td><td>No movement in or out this week</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Staked 30 Aug &ndash; 12 Sep, corporate</td><td class=\"num\">38</td><td class=\"num\">&mdash;</td><td>CanAlaska 16, Skyharbour 6, Gem Oil 6 (excludes 4 further Gem Oil claims in an outlier block ~370&nbsp;km outside the basin, near Flin Flon), Cosa Resources 6, Standard Uranium 4</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Staked 30 Aug &ndash; 12 Sep, individuals</td><td class=\"num\">39</td><td class=\"num\">&mdash;</td><td>22 distinct individual stakers, largest blocks Jade Checlair 5, then Mark Andrews, Sujay Nair, Stan Miller and Tanner Stell 4 each</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Good standing expiring by 19 Sep</td><td class=\"num\">102</td><td class=\"num\">45</td><td>Ryan Kalt (individual) 17, Eagle Plains 13, Murchison Minerals 12, Orano 11, Greenridge Exploration 10, then smaller holders</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Approaching, 20-26 Sep (8-14 days out)</td><td class=\"num\">94</td><td class=\"num\">151</td><td>Holder-by-holder breakdown not yet available</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"note\">\n  <span class=\"h\">Second lapsing tier</span>\n  The map's \"Lapsing Within 7 Days\" layer is joined by \"Lapsing 8-14 Days\" (lighter pink, off by default), extending the good-standing view one tier further out. <b>94 dispositions reach good standing between 20 and 26 September</b>, down from 151 a week ago as part of that group has since rolled into the 7-day tier above. As with the 7-day layer, Saskatchewan does not warn a holder before a claim lapses, so this remains a hard deadline, not a grace period.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"note\">\n  <span class=\"h\">Ground coming open: 102 dispositions inside seven days</span>\n  <b>102 active dispositions reach their good-standing date by 19 September, more than double last week's 45.</b> An individual holder, Ryan Kalt, accounts for the largest single block at 17, followed by Eagle Plains Resources at 13 and Murchison Minerals at 12. Orano Canada has 11, Greenridge Exploration 10, Inspiration Energy 8, and a second individual holder, Jasper jon arthur Mowatt, 5. 92 Energy Canada has 4; Golden Band Resources, Argo Gold, Fathom Minerals and a Denison Mines/Cosa Resources joint holding have 3 each; Debbie Dahrouge (an individual staker), 1255004 B.C. Ltd. and Willgrass Resources have 2 each. The remainder are singles, including a 50/50 pair (randy andrew powder / Steve Alphonse Powder) on one disposition.<br><br>\n  Saskatchewan does not warn a holder before a claim goes: the registry manual states a claim lapses without notice where work credits are short and no deficiency deposit has been made. So the good-standing date is a hard deadline rather than the start of a grace period.\n</div><h2 class=\"sec\">Archive</h2>\n<div class=\"arch\">\n  <div class=\"arow\"><span class=\"ad\">2026-09-12</span><span class=\"cur\">No. 003 · current edition</span><span class=\"as\">Week in review, 6-12 Sep · same six ranked items carry over, no new releases since Purepoint's Nova assay on 10 Sep · 77 new dispositions staked in the trailing 14 days (CanAlaska, Skyharbour, Gem Oil, Cosa Resources, Standard Uranium, plus 22 individual stakers) · lapsed register unchanged · 102 dispositions expiring by 19 Sep, more than double last week</span></div>\n  <a class=\"arow\" href=\"https://basinwatch.ca/archive/edition002/\"><span class=\"ad\">2026-09-11</span><span class=\"as\">No. 002 · Week in review, 5-11 Sep · Purepoint's Nova assay (1.65% U₃O₈/0.3m) leads, IsoEnergy's Larocque East program at #2 · Belmont's Crackingstone gravity survey and Terra North's Charlot-Neely radiometric anomalies new to the ranked list · no new claims staked, lapsed register unchanged · 45 dispositions expiring by 18 Sep</span></a>\n  <a class=\"arow\" href=\"https://basinwatch.ca/archive/edition001/\"><span class=\"ad\">2026-09-10</span><span class=\"as\">No. 001 · Week in review, 4-10 Sep · Purepoint's Nova assay (1.65% U₃O₈/0.3m) takes the lead over IsoEnergy's Larocque East program · 5 items ranked · four new GEM Oil dispositions, all in the same Flin Flon outlier block, 370 km outside the basin · lapsed register unchanged · 49 dispositions expiring by 17 Sep</span></a>\n  </div>"
